      "functional_impact_measured": "Non-permeabilizing confocal immunofluorescence confirmed plasma membrane localisation of both wild-type and Arg394His KCNH7 constructs carrying the tag; channel electrophysiology was not separately reported for the tagged construct in this study.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L1 explicitly states the V5 tag was inserted between amino acids 441 and 442 of the S1-S2 extracellular loop of full-length KCNH7. Python verification confirms position 441 (R) and 442 (R) both fall within the authoritative extracellular span 433-452, 9 residues from the TM1 C-terminus (432) and 12 residues from the TM2 N-terminus (453), both well above the \u22653 aa minimum. Two downstream cysteines (444, 448) are present in the loop but are C-terminal to the insert junction, and the paper demonstrates successful surface trafficking, indicating the tag does not disrupt folding or membrane targeting. Full-length KCNH7 (Kv11.3/ERG3) carrying a V5 epitope tag (GKPIPNPLLGLDST, 14 aa) inserted between residues 441 and 442 in the S1-S2 extracellular loop was expressed in Neuro-2a cells; surface display was assessed by indirect immunofluorescence under non-permeabilizing conditions.",
      "sources": [
